ier on wall-clock time\n- **Fall back**: clocks go back 1 hour → the job runs 1 hour later on wall-clock time\n\n**The fix:** Use a proper scheduler that understands DST, not raw `setInterval`:\n\n```javascript\nconst schedule = require('node-schedule');\nschedule.scheduleJob('0 2 * * *', () => run()); // Every day at 2 AM local time\n```\n\nOr for cron-based scheduling, any library that maps to system cron (which handles DST) will work correctly.\n\n**Why this works:** System schedulers track wall-clock time, not elapsed milliseconds. They automatically adjust when DST changes. `setInterval` can't—it only knows about elapsed time since the job started.","ttft_ms":7870,"type":"result","duration_ms":9920,"uuid":"715fbe5a-3b10-427e-8b20-75b700db3de5","ttft_stream_ms":820,"time_to_request_ms":115,"first_content_frame_ms":821,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":10,"outputTokens":940,"cacheReadInputTokens":7913,"cacheCreationInputTokens":555,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.0066113,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":676,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":555,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"credential_expires_at":"2026-12-12T05:14:51.381Z"}